Don't Mess With Paste
=====================

Makes paste work in Moodle VPL's code editor when "restricted editor" is on,
in Chrome and Firefox. Text is pasted exactly as copied, and copy is left alone.

How it works: VPL replaces the Ace editor's paste with one that discards the
real clipboard. paste-fix.js catches the paste first and runs Ace's own paste
command with the real clipboard text. See
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-23-vpl-paste-fix-design.md.

No build step: the files are plain JavaScript.

Load for testing
----------------
Chrome:  chrome://extensions -> Developer mode -> Load unpacked -> this folder.
Firefox: about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox -> Load Temporary Add-on ->
         manifest.json (Firefox 140 or later).

Package
-------
.\pack-extension.ps1   (writes dist/dont-mess-with-paste-{chrome,firefox}-<version>.zip)

Test
----
Serve the project root over http (python -m http.server 8765) and open
http://localhost:8765/test/vpl-harness.html, and ?fix=0 for the unfixed
control. Every line should read PASS.
